# Response headers for the web client, served as Workers Static Assets.
# The page holds decrypted notes and keys in memory, so only code from this
# origin may run: no inline scripts, no eval, no third-party hosts.
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' lets the browser compile our own WebAssembly
# (Flutter, libsodium, SQLite). The style hashes are the two <style>
# elements Flutter's engine inserts, whose text differs per browser (Chrome,
# Edge, Firefox, Safari) and per build (WebAssembly or JavaScript), plus the
# empty one SelectionArea (the Markdown preview) creates and then fills
# through CSSOM. The page talks to its own origin only: the same Worker
# serves the app and the sync (/api), which sees ciphertext only and streams
# the encrypted recordings to and from R2. test/platform/web_headers_test.dart
# checks it.
